2. THE LOAD BASIS
2a. what _GND_LOADS is: the union of the arriving 5 V rails' own allocations, each at the part its branch returns at (the generator's
    comment of 13 September). Read from the recorded calls, composed through rt500 (with Layer 9's draft in brackets):
      +5V_S1   at J_5V_S1   declared 2.50 A typical, 6.60 A peak; its loads sum 5.341 A (2.50 / 6.60 A, loads 5.341 A)
      +5V_S2   at J_5V_S2   declared 4.20 A typical, 6.60 A peak; its loads sum 5.341 A (4.20 / 6.60 A, loads 5.341 A)
      +5V_S3   at J_5V_S3   declared 2.50 A typical, 6.60 A peak; its loads sum 5.341 A (2.50 / 6.60 A, loads 5.341 A)
      +5V_DEV  at J_5V_DEV  declared 3.80 A typical, 6.00 A peak; its loads sum 5.490 A (3.44 / 6.04 A, loads 5.130 A)
      +5V_IOC  at J_5V_IOC  (Layer 9's draft only: 0.36 A typical, 1.47 A peak, loads 0.360 A)
      the leads' allocations sum to 21.513 A (21.513 A); GND's list sums 21.513 A (21.513 A): the same amperes, EQUAL
      keys the return lists at another part than the supply: F2, F3, U901 on the supply side, J_PANEL, J_QMX, U3, U4 on the return side (a polyfuse or an eFuse has
      no ground pin that carries its load: PANEL_5V returns at J_PANEL, VBUS_QMX at J_QMX, +5V_HDMI's allocation at U3 and U4)
2b. is it the return current? By Kirchhoff the board's return to board A is the sum of what arrives on its leads; the cables that
    leave the board (panel, QMX, camera, LimeSDR, RockBLOCK, HDMI) carry their own return back to this board's ground.
    NAMED TWICE, each judged: J_PANEL and J_QMX are loads of a series segment of the device rail (PANEL_5V, VBUS_QMX), the same current further
    along its own path, listed once in the return, where it comes back. U3 and U4 are also loads of a rail this board converts (+3V3_DEV,
    0.01 A each, inside U25's 5 V input); the return's entries at those two parts are the 0.20 A allocation of the polyfuse F2
    (+5V_HDMI) split in two, another branch's amperes. No ampere is in the return's list twice. (A LOCATION only: +5V_HDMI
    declares its own load at J_HDMI, so that return comes back at the HDMI connector, not at the switches: finding L8R2-F37.)
    THE COOLER BRANCH (the brief's example): the return lists the step-up's 5 V input at U701 (0.69 A; 2.75 W of fan over 0.80 at 5.0 V)
    and NOT the fan's 12 V current (CFAN1_12V's load U702 0.22 A, CFAN1_V's load J_FAN1): 0.22 A leaves at J_FAN1 pin 2 and the
    rest of the 0.69 A at the step-up's ground. One count.
    MISSING: the PoE port's return. +54V_POE (0.30 A typical, 0.60 A peak) arrives on J_54V, whose pin 2 is on GND on both boards;
    the port's current comes back through POE_DRAIN, Q1 and POE_SEN to the sense resistor R12 and enters GND there. The list has
    no entry for it and the declaration does not name J_54V. Corrected by this round's draft (R12 at the rail's peak; J_54V a source).
    RETURNS ELSEWHERE: none found (board B has no second ground and no chassis bond; record l8gnd's GND-002 moves only the
    RJ45 shell and C33 to CHASSIS, which carry no supply current).
2c. the three figures the declaration could hold (A; composed through rt500, with Layer 9's draft in brackets):
    (i) THE SUM OF THE LEADS' DECLARED PEAKS, an UPPER BOUND (every lead at its own peak at once): 26.4000 A (27.9108 A) with the PoE
        lead's 0.60 A; 22.23 A on the committed generator. The typicals sum to 13.30 A (13.30 A). DECLARED.
    (ii) LAYER 9'S BUDGET (the copy of fnd/l9t5 at 841e6c7e, its rounds 4 to 6: PS-ALLTX with the standby card off; the ONE budget
         this record reads since round 8): the four 5.1 V stages' output summed per state, before Layer 9's draft moves the
