4. THE JUDGMENT
   (a) THE DECLARATION IS WRONG, and is corrected (round 7, section 5). Its peak was a typed sum of the leads' peaks that went stale
       twice; its typical 10.0 A is under the leads' own 13.30 A; its sources omit J_54V. The basis supports: typical 13.30 A and peak
       26.40 A (27.9108 A with Layer 9's draft), derived in the generator from the leads' declarations, the peak an UPPER BOUND.
   (b) THE LOAD LIST IS RIGHT IN WHAT IT COUNTS AND MISSED ONE RETURN: no ampere is counted twice and none returns elsewhere; the PoE
       port's 0.60 A at R12 is added. The device rail's shortfall against C-DEV rev 1 is I-03 (Layer 9's draft, which now declares
       the device lead's peak from its basis, 6.0359 A).
   (c) THE RETURN PATH AS DRAWN DOES NOT HOLD: a circuit defect of the A to B interface, finding L8R2-F31, OPEN. With every vertex of
       the permitted contact resistances enumerated (round 7 had sampled six and missed the worst), on C-DEV rev 1 a 5 V lead's pin 2
       reaches 12.092 A against its printed 10 A and a ribbon conductor 2.672 A against its printed 1 A (3d). These are the MODEL's
       answers on the makers' printed limits: no harness exists and no contact has been measured.
   (d) THE CORRECTION IS DRAFTED, NOT ACCEPTED: a dedicated ground return of 3 XT60 leads (6 conductors of 12 AWG) between the two
       boards, drawn on both generators (section 5) and verified over every vertex with its own terminations at their printed
       limit (section 6), on the declared upper bound: a VH pin 2 at most 4.927 A against JST's printed 10 A (AWG 16, standard
       header); a ribbon conductor at most 0.635 A against Wurth's printed 1 A at 25 C (0.488 A at the inside air against at least
       0.5995 A there, INFERRED); an XT60 contact at most 11.031 A against Amass's printed 30 A (V1.2) and 35 A MAX with 12 AWG at a
       rise under 85 C (2021V1), at least 25.11 A at the inside air (INFERRED); the ground shift at most 11.42 mV against 0.9418 V.
       L8R2-F31 STAYS OPEN until an independent check has read the changed design; what the rows rest on that no maker prints
       is listed in 6d and is not hidden by this arithmetic.
   NOT RAISED TO MAKE THE GENERATOR PASS: the declaration is derived, the same text reads 22.23 A on the committed generator, a lead
       declared lower lowers it.

