6d. WHAT THE ROWS REST ON THAT NO MAKER PRINTS, each named with its dependence:
    - the plane copper in series with the return bundle (P0 round, V6-B1, 5 October 2026): every row takes each board as one node;
      the plane resistance between the return sockets' lands and the 5 V entries is a NAMED CONDITION, L8R2-F33a, with the bound
      each case tolerates and the land separation a layout may have on the declared stackups in l8r2_p0.out section 2
      (PROVISIONAL on the routed boards' extraction). After the focused check cx45 (Q2) the sockets are PLACED with their
      courtyards on both boards and the return studied as a distributed network (l8r2_dist.out) on a stand-in XT60-M land,
      assumed sites and fill and an averaged LDO probe: every printed row holds there and the service cases hold on the least
      ratings, a STUDY, not a correction; after cx46 V6-B1 stays OPEN as REMAINING ENGINEERING (the selected XT60-F lands, the
      real source and load sites, a justified distributed resistance with tolerance coverage, each LDO's own shift).
    - the XT60's contact resistance after ageing. Amass prints one limit (1.0 mOhm, 2021V1) with a 100-cycle life and no separate
      after-test figure. Every row still holds on the printed ratings while each XT60 contact stays at or under 2.06 mOhm, and on
      the least ratings at or under 1.43 mOhm (2.1 and 1.4 times the printed limit). Beyond that a row fails: a four-wire reading of the
      return leads at assembly and in service is what would show it.
    - the contacts' minimum resistance: none is printed, so every row takes the branch's own contacts at 0 (the most adverse).
    - the derating at the inside air: none is printed, so every row carries the least rating consistent with its sheet beside
      the printed one (3b); the VH's rests on the ASSUMPTION that its rating is stated at 25 C.
    - the wires' own resistance: MODEL figures from nominal sections and lengths (no wire part is named, L8R2-F34), and the ribbon's
      is its maker's MAXIMUM. With each branch's own wire at 0.82 of its figure (ASSUMPTION, WIRE_FLOOR) the maxima become: a VH
      pin 2 5.7851 A, a ribbon conductor 0.7708 A (0.5930 A at the inside air against at least 0.5995 A), an XT60 contact 12.3801 A: every
      row on the printed ratings: yes; on the least ratings: yes.
    - the lengths: the return leads at 150 mm and J_AB2's ribbon at 80 mm are ASSUMPTIONS (Layer 7 routes them).
